src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:3:excerpt: "AI workflows compound when intent, plans, execution, review, and evidence survive outside the chat transcript."
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:20:leaderTakeaway: "Treat agentic work as a workflow OS. Route by uncertainty and risk, scale autonomy by tier, and make evidence part of the deliverable."
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:22:seoDescription: "A web-native walkthrough of artifact-first agentic operations: triage, planning artifacts, autonomy tiers, execution graphs, review gates, and evidence loops."
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:64:| First artifact | Does the task need a PRD, storyboard, research memo, progress file, evidence bundle, or something else? |
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:77:It has no native notion of ownership, dependency, review intensity, or completion evidence. It does not know that a feasibility question should stop before implementation. It does not know that a high-risk migration should trigger a hard boundary before edits. It does not know which facts should become reusable context and which are just scaffolding from the current run.
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:79:The <Term id="artifact-graph">**artifact graph**</Term> is the opposite: a typed set of durable objects that the workflow can resume from and reviewers can validate against. In my current system, that graph includes exploration charters, feasibility briefs, feature contracts, PRDs, implementation plans, decision blocks, progress files, validation records, run evidence, and knowledge handoffs.
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:107:| Already planned phase execution | `/dev:execute-phase` | Updated progress and evidence |
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:133:| Progress File | Store current execution state and evidence. |
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:221:It is done when the system can explain what happened, why it happened, what passed, what failed, what remains, and what should be reusable. That is why progress and evidence are not cleanup. They are the product of the run.
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:223:For my workflows, the evidence stack looks like this:
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:229:| Run intelligence | Session traces, failures, ownership, time, evidence links. |
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:236:  src="/assets/posts/agentic-operations-flow/evidence-stack.jpg"
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:237:  alt="Generated illustration of layered evidence artifacts flowing into a reusable knowledge graph."
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:271:That is the simplest version of the argument. A transcript can be useful during the moment of work, but it is weak operating state. It does not naturally preserve decisions, dependencies, artifacts, review intensity, evidence, or reusable knowledge.
src/content/posts/agentic-operations-flow.mdx:273:An artifact graph does. It lets human intent become reviewable, agent execution become resumable, and evidence become part of the deliverable rather than a screenshot pasted into a status update.
