/Users/miethe/dev/WIP/agents/theses/registry-wave/reg-wave-review-v4/registry_wave_experience_v2/03_NAVIGATION_AND_STATE_CONTRACT.md:114:Only one modal DOM node is open at a time. A logical parent stack is permitted. Store each parent's scroll and local expansion state before replacing the host. Restoring an evidence view must restore open receipts, not recreate a collapsed set at the top.
/Users/miethe/dev/WIP/agents/theses/registry-wave/reg-wave-review-v4/registry_wave_experience_v2/03_NAVIGATION_AND_STATE_CONTRACT.md:118:Opening a substantial detail view focuses a programmatically focusable title near the start. No giant `aria-describedby` wrapping all structured content. Tab stays inside the modal. Escape and visible close are equivalent one-level return actions. A separate “Back to essay” exits the full inspection chain. For a direct route, there is no modal trap and no simulated prior reading state [W3C-01].
/Users/miethe/dev/WIP/agents/theses/registry-wave/reg-wave-review-v4/registry_wave_experience_v2/03_NAVIGATION_AND_STATE_CONTRACT.md:120:Opening a focus view from another focus view requires an explicit click. No automatic dialog from scrolling, no focus moves during reading, no auto-open receipt and no auto-swapping images. Backdrop clicks may close Figure Viewer; for full Thread/Evidence views, keep the default conservative (visible Close or Escape), avoiding accidental dismissal during reading.

