   400	      });

codex
The root cause is now concrete: `restoreRoot()` computes and clamps the target immediately after `dialog.close()`, while the fixed-body lock and modal state still leave the document at viewport height. The clamp therefore converts a valid saved anchor position to zero. I’ll defer restoration until post-close layout is measurable, add an explicit dialog focus loop, and then use a DOM-width walk to localize the narrow-viewport overflow before styling it.
